upstream/minhook/

  MinHook, the minimalistic x86/x64 API hooking library for Windows.

  Origin:   https://github.com/TsudaKageyu/minhook
  Version:  1.3.4 (tag v1.3.4, commit c3fcafdc10146beb5919319d0683e44e3c30d537)
  Licence:  BSD-2-Clause (upstream/minhook/LICENSE.txt), including the
            Hacker Disassembler Engine under src/hde/ (same file).
  Imported: LICENSE.txt, AUTHORS.txt, include/, and src/, byte for byte.
            Upstream's build files were left out.
  Changes:  None. Everything the package needs on top of upstream is ours
            and lives in the package: libcompanion/minhook/buildfile and
            libcompanion/minhook/compat/windows.h.

  Exception: this is a bundled dependency, contrary to the "no bundled
  dependencies" rule (charter 2.2, rule 3; [PKG] 3.5), and it was granted as
  an explicit exception on 2026-09-27.

  Reason: the companion is built for Windows (the 64-bit Steam client) and
  for Linux (the 32-bit native Steam client). On Windows it uses MinHook as a
  whole. On Linux it uses only MinHook's instruction length decoder (HDE) for
  its own detour, which requires building HDE against a stand-in for
  <windows.h>. The libminhook package on cppget.org builds for Windows only
  and doesn't expose HDE, so it can serve neither the Linux build nor the
  stand-in.

  Removal: the exception ends once a package provides HDE for every target
  the companion is built for. The vendored copy is then deleted and replaced
  with a depends: value.

  Updating: replace the imported files with those of a newer upstream tag,
  byte for byte, and update the version above.
